# Shell scripts run under bash in CI. A CRLF checkout turns the shebang and
# `set -euo pipefail` lines into syntax errors, so force LF for them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Node scripts under scripts/ are run directly (`node scripts/...`) and one is
# imported by vitest. Vite's SSR transform prepends imports to the module, so a
# CRLF checkout leaves the shebang line unrecognized and the suite dies with
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" (seen on a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true). Keep them LF like the shell scripts.
*.mjs text eol=lf

# CHANGELOG.md is an append-only list: every PR adds entries, so every PR
# edits the same lines and conflicts with every other PR. The union driver
# keeps added lines from both sides instead of conflict markers, which is
# semantically correct here because both entries are true. Scope is this
# file ONLY: never apply union (or ours/theirs) to code, where "both" can
# silently drop a fix or weaken a gate. Limit, stated honestly: GitHub's
# server-side merges may ignore .gitattributes drivers, so the real fix
# for the CHANGELOG race is changelog.d fragments (see gitops §6) — the
# union line only helps local merges and rebases.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
